  * \return the tolerance of the comparisons of the computations using
  * kernels or the behaviours generated by the generic-parallel interface to
  * the reference computations. In float, the relative differences reach
- * 3.7e-4 (behaviours in finite strain, whose Newton algorithm stops at a
- * relative residual of 4e-4) and 1.9e-3 with the tangent operator applied
- * without assembly (conjugate gradient with a Jacobi preconditioner
- * stopping at a relative residual of 1.2e-5)
+ * 4.0e-4 with an assembled tangent operator (behaviours in finite strain,
+ * whose Newton algorithm stops at a relative residual of 4e-4). With the
+ * tangent operator applied without assembly (conjugate gradient with a
+ * Jacobi preconditioner stopping at a relative residual of 1.2e-5), they
+ * reach 5.1e-4 in parallel, the reference being computed by MUMPS, and
+ * 6.3e-3 in sequential, the reference being then computed by GMRES with a
+ * Jacobi preconditioner, MFEM in single precision having no sequential
+ * direct solver (see `SequentialLinearSolver.hxx`)
  * \param[in] opts: options of the computation
  */
 static mfem_mgis::real getComparisonTolerance(const ComputationOptions& opts) {
   if (opts.matrix_free) {
-    return mfem_mgis::unit_tests::tolerance(1e-10, 2e-2);
+    return parallel ? mfem_mgis::unit_tests::tolerance(1e-10, 5e-3)
+                    : mfem_mgis::unit_tests::tolerance(1e-10, 6e-2);
   }
   return mfem_mgis::unit_tests::tolerance(1e-10, 4e-3);
 }  // end of getComparisonTolerance
